      "description": "You know the temperature. What you actually want to know is whether they need the pramsuit.\n\nTots Weather turns the local forecast into a straight answer: what to dress your child in right now, for what you're about to do. It knows the difference between a newborn in a pram and a toddler walking to nursery, between 8°C in still air and 8°C in a north wind, and between a bedroom at 17°C and one at 22°C.\n\nWHAT IT TELLS YOU\n\n• The outfit, layer by layer, in plain UK terms. Vest, sleepsuit, pramsuit, wellies.\n• Bedtime: which tog sleeping bag for tonight's room temperature, and what to wear underneath. Tell it which bags you own and it only ever suggests those.\n• Your child, drawn in exactly that outfit, so it's clear at a glance.\n• While you're out: what to take off or add as the day changes, what to bring for later, and when to put sun cream on and top it up, with a reminder at each change.\n• Tonight's room: once it has learnt how your room follows the weather, it forecasts the bedroom at bedtime and the sleeping bag to match. The thermometer at bedtime still has the final say.\n• How they're travelling: a sling strips the bulky suit and warms the extremities; a car seat insists the coat comes off before the straps go on.\n• The best window for a walk today, from the hours they're actually awake.\n• A packing list for the bag, generated from the day ahead.\n• Tomorrow, tonight, so you can lay clothes out before bed.\n• A morning briefing and a heads-up before rain, if you want them.\n\nBUILT FOR EVERYONE WHO LOOKS AFTER THEM\n\nChildren, places and the nursery temperature stay in step on every phone you invite: a partner, grandparent or childminder. Add the Home Screen widget and the answer is there without opening anything.\n\nGUIDANCE, NOT MEDICAL ADVICE\n\nThe advice follows published UK guidance, and every source is named in the app with a link: The Lullaby Trust for safer sleep and room temperature, the NHS for fever and sun safety, the T.I.C.K.S. rule for slings, Good Egg for car seats. Tog ratings come from sleeping-bag manufacturers' charts.\n\nTots Weather can't see your child and can't tell how well or unwell they are. If you're worried about your child, contact your health visitor, GP, or NHS 111. In an emergency, call 999.\n\nPRIVACY\n\nNo ads, no analytics, no tracking, and nothing about your family is ever sold or shared.",
